{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache and As Daylight Dies feel like natural next choices because their heavy riffs and melodic vocals connect with what I enjoy in In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Undertow feels especially relevant after 10.000 Days because I want to explore more of Tool's heavy, intricate sound; Vol. 3 also fits my interest in aggression balanced with melody."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Decemberunderground feels less suited to this session because its emo and electronic textures do not satisfy my current appetite for heavy riffs.",
    "Iv gives me too little information to judge whether it fits, so I would pass rather than assume I would enjoy it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in melodic hard rock seems to carry too much weight today: We Are Not Alone and Phobia fit my broader taste, but I currently want something heavier.",
    "Being associated with the same broad rock and metal listening territory is not enough; I care about how the riffs, vocals, and melodies work together."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choice of 10.000 Days makes exploring more Tool particularly appealing right now.",
    "There is a difference between music I generally like and music I would choose this session: City of Evil and Mezmerize appeal to me, but The End of Heartache and Undertow give me stronger reasons to listen now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my taste for heavy music with melody, but give less weight to my current preference for heavier riffs and further exploration of Tool."
}"}
